## Open chores

(none)

Completed chores collapse to one archive line each, in this form (Part 5b). `DONE` is the
first token after the colon because that is what the git hooks read: a chore branch that
touches a role path may only merge when the same commit records its completion here.
The example uses `CHORE-NNN` on purpose: the rule requires DIGITS, so this line is a shape
you copy rather than a record the hooks would count. An example that counts as a real record
would ship every new instance a pre-satisfied one.

